WEBVTT

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
kanashige ni saku hana ni kimi no omokage wo mita

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
I saw your image in the flower that is blossoming sorrowfully

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
daisuki na ame nanoni naze ka kyou wa tsumetakute

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
I love rain, yet it felt frosty today

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
kisetsu wa meguri mori wa somerare kaze wa kanadete omoi afurete

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
The season changed, the forest was colored, the wind played a tune, memories overflowed

00:37.600 --> 00:46.786
tsuki no kakera wo atsumete yume wo kazari nemuru

00:37.600 --> 00:46.787
Gather the pieces of the moon, decorate the dream and sleep

00:47.020 --> 00:56.153
toki no suna chiribametemo ano koro e kaeranai

00:47.020 --> 00:56.154
Even if I sprinkle the sand of time, I cannot return to the past

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
ikiru imi sageshiteiru dare mo mina tabibito

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
Those searching for the meaning of life are all travellers

01:05.769 --> 01:14.817
haruka naru tabiji tadori boku wa ima arukidasu

01:05.776 --> 01:14.817
I set my course on this endless journey

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
ibara no michi no mukou e...

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
for the place beyond the thorny path...

01:25.812 --> 01:30.732
The artist of life who produces miracles
with his godlike scalpel skills.

01:31.651 --> 01:33.986
The surgeon whom the era has yearned for.

01:34.862 --> 01:35.905
Black Jack.

02:03.326 --> 02:06.473
Originally "Dingo" by Tezuka Osamu

02:03.326 --> 02:06.473
A Contagious Disease in the Wild

02:13.809 --> 02:17.603
Look Doc, there are so many kangaroos out there.

02:18.022 --> 02:21.519
Being in a kangaroo's pocket,

02:21.775 --> 02:24.610
hugging a koala,

02:24.695 --> 02:26.946
and swimming with a duckbill platypus!

02:26.947 --> 02:29.339
Pinoco, we're not here to have fun.

02:29.742 --> 02:33.494
Doc, is the patient's place still far away?

02:33.537 --> 02:37.075
It will take us a while to get to the Carreras Ranch.

02:37.416 --> 02:42.211
Then let's finish it up quickly and go see koalas!

02:43.297 --> 02:44.726
Yes!

02:45.549 --> 02:49.747
<i>We're suffering from high fevers as we speak.</i>

02:50.637 --> 02:52.847
<i>Your operation failed!</i>

02:52.848 --> 02:53.581
<i>Impossible!</i>

02:53.766 --> 02:55.308
<i>The operation went perfectly!</i>

02:55.309 --> 02:58.726
<i>Many doctors have examined me, but
nobody can figure anything out.</i>

02:58.896 --> 03:02.273
<i>On top of it, now I'm getting red spots all over my body.</i>

03:03.358 --> 03:05.526
<i>Red spots?</i>

03:05.527 --> 03:07.570
<i>Anyway, get here immediately!</i>

03:07.571 --> 03:10.179
<i>Or else, I'll make it an international issue!</i>

03:12.534 --> 03:14.982
Doc, look!

03:19.333 --> 03:22.960
There must be many koalas and kangaroos there!

03:22.961 --> 03:24.378
I want to go!

03:24.546 --> 03:25.379
Don't joke around.

03:25.380 --> 03:26.672
We're here for a job.

03:26.673 --> 03:29.008
Please!

03:29.093 --> 03:30.343
Hey! Pinoco!

03:30.344 --> 03:31.761
Let's go!

03:39.144 --> 03:40.102
Thanks.

03:40.103 --> 03:41.604
No problem!

03:41.605 --> 03:43.523
I'll take good care of your daughter!

03:43.732 --> 03:44.934
No.

03:45.150 --> 03:47.985
I'm Doc's wife.

03:48.152 --> 03:49.395
Wife?

03:49.822 --> 03:52.374
Depending on the situation, I may
not be back for two or three days.

03:52.699 --> 03:55.451
Once you're done here, wait for me at the hotel.

03:55.619 --> 03:57.411
Aye-aye!

03:57.621 --> 03:59.997
Let's go see the koalas!

03:59.998 --> 04:01.415
W-wait up!

04:14.680 --> 04:16.722
W-w-wow! Don't go inside the fence!

04:16.723 --> 04:19.934
Wait up!

04:20.227 --> 04:22.705
Hello there, koalas.

04:22.938 --> 04:26.357
Can I hold her too?

04:26.358 --> 04:28.401
Hey! Don't climb the tree!

04:28.402 --> 04:29.986
Just a little bit?

04:42.374 --> 04:45.501
I've driven for five straight hours and still no gas station.

04:54.219 --> 04:55.928
I'm running low on gas.

05:00.642 --> 05:01.392
<i>What happened?</i>

05:07.065 --> 05:08.317
<i>Are they dead?</i>

05:35.969 --> 05:37.236
Mr. Carreras!

05:38.263 --> 05:39.722
Anybody home?!

05:47.189 --> 05:47.897
Hey!

05:48.315 --> 05:49.398
What are you doing here?

05:56.156 --> 05:57.073
That's...

05:57.908 --> 06:00.034
Heart failure?

06:00.452 --> 06:03.503
Or was it brain damage from some type
of strong poisonous substance?

06:06.083 --> 06:08.229
Are you the doctor he was waiting for?

06:08.710 --> 06:09.794
You're too late.

06:09.795 --> 06:12.380
He had a seizure just a little while ago.

06:12.714 --> 06:13.644
And who are you?

06:14.132 --> 06:16.342
I was employed by him.

06:17.135 --> 06:19.303
I'm the only one left here now.

06:19.763 --> 06:22.931
Even all the sheep and horses
died from this creepy disease.

06:23.266 --> 06:25.590
The doctors themselves got scared
and hightailed it out of here.

06:25.936 --> 06:27.770
Wait! Where are you going?

06:27.771 --> 06:28.354
Let me go!

06:28.897 --> 06:29.522
Let go of me!

06:32.150 --> 06:32.942
You too?

06:34.528 --> 06:35.611
Hey! Wait!

06:45.539 --> 06:47.083
Hey! Where are you going?!

06:47.374 --> 06:49.503
I don't wanna die here!

06:50.012 --> 06:50.888
I'm gonna escape!

06:50.919 --> 06:51.836
Running away, man!

06:52.003 --> 06:53.087
Wait!

06:53.088 --> 06:55.121
There's a good chance you're infected too!

07:29.082 --> 07:30.841
<i>Damn! I'm out of gas!</i>

07:35.255 --> 07:37.636
The koalas were so cute.

07:37.799 --> 07:39.592
Now, let's head to the hotel.

07:39.593 --> 07:41.302
Not to the hotel.

07:41.303 --> 07:43.345
Go to the patient's house.

07:43.346 --> 07:44.513
The patient?

07:44.668 --> 07:46.570
Just go.

07:46.808 --> 07:48.017
Fine, fine.

07:48.018 --> 07:50.477
So, where do I need to go?

07:50.642 --> 07:54.106
For now, keep driving straight.

07:54.983 --> 07:55.937
What's the address?

07:56.359 --> 07:57.401
I don't know.

07:58.987 --> 08:00.045
What's their name?

08:02.032 --> 08:03.449
I forgot.

08:14.336 --> 08:15.747
It's completely out of gas.

08:17.047 --> 08:18.052
This is as far as I go.

08:25.347 --> 08:28.101
Damn, there's still 500 km until town.

08:41.363 --> 08:42.529
Wait there for a minute!

08:42.530 --> 08:44.281
I'm going to buy ice cream!

08:45.575 --> 08:46.902
Give me a break!

08:47.077 --> 08:48.744
I don't want to go any further!

08:54.793 --> 08:56.418
I'm back!

09:02.967 --> 09:05.386
Ohmigewdness!

09:13.311 --> 09:15.060
I guess I was being too optimistic.

09:15.355 --> 09:19.119
I was hoping that a car or a private
plane would go by, but...

09:27.867 --> 09:30.369
Doc, where are you?

09:31.079 --> 09:33.349
Doc!

09:36.960 --> 09:38.502
What?

09:54.185 --> 09:56.061
Oh?

10:03.570 --> 10:06.488
O-o-o-oh God!

10:25.037 --> 10:27.080
That was really close.

10:27.239 --> 10:30.166
You scared me even more.

10:30.167 --> 10:32.168
I thought you were a lion or a bear or something.

10:32.378 --> 10:33.886
Sorry about that.

10:36.548 --> 10:40.917
I called the hotel, but your companion isn't back yet.

10:42.971 --> 10:45.848
I asked them to relay the message, so it should be fine.

10:46.314 --> 10:49.402
What were you doing back there?

10:49.645 --> 10:53.621
I was patrolling for dingos, which are wolf-like creatures.

10:56.582 --> 10:57.568
Dingos?

11:02.908 --> 11:04.192
Largo?

11:06.787 --> 11:09.789
This is Fol, my partner.

11:14.586 --> 11:18.222
I think Doc's hopelessly lost without me,

11:18.222 --> 11:20.921
so can you look for him with me?

11:21.051 --> 11:25.019
But it's difficult without knowing his patient's name.

11:28.559 --> 11:30.434
Don't worry.

11:30.435 --> 11:32.478
I'll ask around to all my friends.

11:32.813 --> 11:33.511
OK.

11:45.868 --> 11:49.330
The dingos aren't around today...

11:49.872 --> 11:52.832
Are dingos that bad of an animal?

11:53.625 --> 11:57.461
Yes, for those of us who own ranches.

11:58.380 --> 12:02.425
Dingos were brought here by people long ago,

12:03.844 --> 12:05.386
then they returned to being wild,

12:06.763 --> 12:10.298
and started attacking people and cattle.

12:13.645 --> 12:17.857
That's why we patrol for them in the morning and evening.

12:18.650 --> 12:19.807
Oh, Fol.

12:20.777 --> 12:22.862
Hey, that tickles!

12:23.947 --> 12:25.489
Wait! Wait!

12:26.575 --> 12:27.867
Come play with me!

12:29.328 --> 12:33.831
I just wish dingos and people could be friends like you two!

12:43.175 --> 12:48.849
<i>On this nameless planet, I walk on an endless road.</i>

12:57.731 --> 13:00.108
<i>I cure my hunger with grasses clustered along the path,</i>

13:01.693 --> 13:04.002
<i>and sleep while the breeze of the wilderness caresses me.</i>

13:04.488 --> 13:05.907
<i>There is no time to relax.</i>

13:18.168 --> 13:21.877
<i>At 13:20, I feel an acute pain in my lower left abdomen.</i>

13:22.089 --> 13:24.131
<i>I recover from it an hour later.</i>

13:31.056 --> 13:36.102
<i>The same day, at 18:40, I feel a dull
pain in my lower right abdomen.</i>

13:36.103 --> 13:37.084
I have a slight fever too.

13:38.271 --> 13:41.273
<i>It could be appendicitis or perforated pan-peritonitis.</i>

13:43.819 --> 13:45.449
<i>I examined myself with the instruments I had.</i>

13:46.113 --> 13:48.197
<i>But there are no abnormalities.</i>

13:52.911 --> 13:56.163
<i>I injected myself with an antibiotic, but it didn't help.</i>

14:01.878 --> 14:02.986
5:30.

14:03.380 --> 14:07.133
<i>The abdominal pain has gone away, but I've
had a high fever since early this morning.</i>

14:07.384 --> 14:09.080
<i>I can't move well either.</i>

14:12.264 --> 14:13.301
Could it be...

14:13.598 --> 14:19.436
Carrots and potatoes, all simmering in a pot.

14:19.437 --> 14:23.661
Put in some curry powder and simmer it some more.

14:23.900 --> 14:25.359
Just wait a bit longer, Fol.

14:25.360 --> 14:28.237
I'm making some yummy curry rice.

14:28.947 --> 14:29.914
Curry?

14:30.448 --> 14:33.284
...to the Carreras Ranch.

14:34.578 --> 14:35.494
Curry!

14:35.495 --> 14:36.662
Carreras!

14:37.038 --> 14:38.164
Yay!

14:38.165 --> 14:39.987
I remembered!

14:41.293 --> 14:43.210
What's all the yelling about?

14:43.211 --> 14:44.336
Carreras!

14:44.671 --> 14:49.425
The name of the patient Doc went to see was Carreras!

14:49.843 --> 14:51.097
Carreras?

14:51.428 --> 14:55.408
I think he has a ranch 300 km south of here.

15:06.693 --> 15:07.484
<i>These are...</i>

15:08.570 --> 15:10.195
<i>the same red spots!</i>

15:10.906 --> 15:13.167
<i>I knew it was contagious.</i>

15:13.408 --> 15:14.745
<i>And now I'm...</i>

15:15.452 --> 15:17.504
<i>Damn! What is this?!</i>

15:18.830 --> 15:19.571
<i>Ouch!</i>

15:20.123 --> 15:22.499
<i>What's happening inside of me?</i>

15:29.049 --> 15:30.787
<i>Think!</i>

15:31.801 --> 15:33.279
<i>Think calmly!</i>

15:39.267 --> 15:41.278
<i>Left first, then right.</i>

15:41.561 --> 15:42.914
<i>The pain moves around.</i>

15:43.313 --> 15:44.801
<i>I've never had such symptoms.</i>

15:46.816 --> 15:48.273
<i>Will I die here?</i>

16:00.997 --> 16:02.373
<i>It moves?</i>

16:05.752 --> 16:08.165
<i>My assumption was very wrong!</i>

16:08.588 --> 16:09.723
<i>I must reexamine my analysis.</i>

16:19.683 --> 16:20.516
<i>Just as I thought.</i>

16:20.517 --> 16:22.712
<i>This is a piece of some organism.</i>

16:24.437 --> 16:26.021
<i>It's an echinococcus!</i>

16:26.439 --> 16:27.648
<i>I get it!</i>

16:27.941 --> 16:31.652
<i>The abdominal pain and the fever were all caused by it!</i>

16:33.488 --> 16:37.371
A parasite was moving around, trying
to pierce through my stomach!

16:39.244 --> 16:42.686
Yeah, let me know if you hear anything.

16:44.273 --> 16:45.207
It's no good.

16:45.208 --> 16:49.795
He said that they haven't had any contact
with Carreras for two or three days.

16:51.714 --> 16:55.055
Maybe something's happened to Doc.

16:58.035 --> 17:04.117
<i>It produces red spots, moves around the host's
body, and secretes a poisonous substance.</i>

17:05.979 --> 17:07.821
<i>This is a new type of echinococcus.</i>

17:08.606 --> 17:12.470
<i>That's why they couldn't figure out
what it was at the local hospital.</i>

17:15.947 --> 17:21.003
<i>At 24:15, I initiated an open abdominal operation
to extirpate the echinococcus.</i>

17:24.330 --> 17:28.584
<i>I'd never dreamed I'd be operating
on myself in a,place likes this.</i>

17:30.587 --> 17:31.822
<i>Begin the operation.</i>

17:47.478 --> 17:49.897
<i>How I wish Pinoco was with me!</i>

17:52.192 --> 17:52.858
<i>Is this it?</i>

18:01.451 --> 18:02.588
<i>Just stay in there.</i>

18:02.869 --> 18:04.147
<i>I'll drag you out of there soon enough.</i>

18:08.875 --> 18:10.543
<i>It should be behind the peritoneum.</i>

18:12.045 --> 18:15.306
<i>It's in my body, so I know where it is.</i>

18:19.010 --> 18:20.010
<i>What's this?</i>

18:20.637 --> 18:21.408
<i>It's huge!</i>

18:26.517 --> 18:28.006
<i>This is the one!</i>

18:36.027 --> 18:37.486
<i>I'm safe now.</i>

18:39.072 --> 18:39.947
<i>What's that?!</i>

18:55.004 --> 18:56.171
<i>They're dingos!</i>

19:03.930 --> 19:07.683
<i>Damn, they smelled my blood and followed it here.</i>

19:12.188 --> 19:14.037
Just stay there.

19:14.482 --> 19:16.735
I'll play with you as much as you want once I'm done.

19:22.865 --> 19:26.886
<i>If they attack all at once, I'm done for.</i>

19:43.761 --> 19:45.522
I'll be done with the stitching soon.

19:45.847 --> 19:46.888
Wait until then!

20:22.508 --> 20:23.717
Doc!

20:24.635 --> 20:25.712
Pinoco!

20:26.220 --> 20:29.848
Doc! What are you doing here?!

20:31.767 --> 20:34.561
He's stitching his own belly!

20:35.229 --> 20:36.753
Operation completed.

20:42.862 --> 20:49.117
The cause of the epidemic in the southern region,
which caused the deaths of twenty-two victims,

20:49.118 --> 20:51.557
has been identified to be a mutated
form of the parasite echinococcus;

20:51.787 --> 20:54.748
the mutation was caused by its encounter
with strong farm chemicals.

20:55.249 --> 21:00.840
This aggressive type secretes a strong
poison inside the animals it infects.

21:01.255 --> 21:03.264
It was first spread by wild dingos,

21:03.507 --> 21:10.325
and was spread even further by the irrigation systems
on farms-this caused a widespread outbreak.

21:18.481 --> 21:19.522
I really appreciate this.

21:19.523 --> 21:23.109
You helped us a lot already and now here
you are taking us to the airport.

21:23.110 --> 21:24.778
Don't mention it.

21:24.779 --> 21:27.948
To those of us who live here, you're a lifesaver.

21:28.908 --> 21:33.286
Anyway, those damn dingos are spreading diseases!

21:34.455 --> 21:37.606
But are the dingos really to blame?

21:39.669 --> 21:42.962
What people left behind has come back to attack us.

21:44.590 --> 21:46.240
That's ironic.

21:48.552 --> 21:53.390
Hey, you can come visit Largo with Fol.

21:53.975 --> 21:56.059
Sure, I'd love to.

21:56.060 --> 21:57.852
Yay!

22:07.077 --> 22:19.032
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

22:07.077 --> 22:19.032
daisukuyo anata to hitotsu ni nareru no nara

22:19.150 --> 22:24.149
I couldn't be happier...

22:19.150 --> 22:24.149
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

22:25.718 --> 22:31.187
I wanted to see you forever

22:25.718 --> 22:31.187
zutto aitakute mattetano

22:31.731 --> 22:37.189
I'm laying on the grill,

22:31.731 --> 22:37.189
ami no ue ni yasashiku nekasete

22:37.793 --> 22:40.278
being heated up by you,

22:37.793 --> 22:40.278
anata ni hoterasarete

22:40.487 --> 22:48.264
so much that I change color

22:40.487 --> 22:48.264
atashi wa iro ga kawarukurai

22:48.349 --> 23:00.118
I dress up with sparkly grains of decorations

22:48.349 --> 23:00.118
kirakira hikaru tsubu no kazari de oshare

23:00.326 --> 23:12.057
I love you darling. Please love me more and more...

23:00.326 --> 23:12.057
daisukiyo motto motto atashi wo aishite

23:12.297 --> 23:23.648
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

23:12.297 --> 23:23.648
daisukiyo anata to hitotsu no nareru no nara

23:23.834 --> 23:28.755
I couldn't be happier

23:23.834 --> 23:28.755
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

23:28.983 --> 23:33.917
How does it taste?

23:28.983 --> 23:33.916
oaji wa ikaga?

23:45.054 --> 24:15.083
Arranging the Flower of Life

23:45.178 --> 23:46.286
A year is all I ask for!

23:46.484 --> 23:47.758
Please save Sono!

23:48.013 --> 23:48.720
The flower...

23:49.048 --> 23:51.766
I want to become the head of this school before I die.

23:52.265 --> 23:54.532
My daughter is sensitive to light.

23:54.778 --> 23:57.347
When she's exposed to sunlight, her skin burns.

23:57.817 --> 24:00.443
and her life is shortened.

24:00.525 --> 24:02.074
I'm dying, right?

24:02.407 --> 24:03.711
How can you assume that?!

24:03.923 --> 24:04.923
Ta-da!

24:06.590 --> 24:08.057
I want to live.

24:08.410 --> 24:09.498
Pinoco, let's begin.

24:09.663 --> 24:10.499
Sono-san...

24:11.566 --> 24:14.155
Next Karte - Arranging the Flower of Life.

24:16.149 --> 24:17.774
Karte NG...

24:20.611 --> 24:21.411
That's...

24:21.654 --> 24:22.648
Is he dead?

24:23.772 --> 24:24.473
Sorry.
